---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy"
  description="How Model Fieldnotes handles preferences and website hosting."
>
  <div class="shell page-content">
    <header class="page-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">A small footprint</p>
      <h1>Privacy.</h1>
    </header>
    <div class="prose standalone-prose">
      <h2>What this website stores</h2>
      <p>
        This site does not run behavioral analytics, advertising scripts,
        tracking pixels, or an email signup service. There are no reader
        accounts. Fonts and images are served with the site.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you change the color theme, your browser saves that preference
        locally under <code>mfn-theme</code>. It is not sent to Model
        Fieldnotes. The site works when local storage is unavailable. Search
        filters stay in the page URL so you can bookmark them.
      </p>
      <h2>Hosting and external links</h2>
      <p>
        GitHub Pages hosts this website. GitHub may process technical request
        information, including IP addresses, to operate and secure its services.
        See{' '}
        <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">
          GitHub’s privacy statement
        </a>
        .
      </p>
      <p>
        Opening GitHub, a research paper, or another external source takes you
        to a service with its own practices. RSS readers retrieve the feed
        without creating an account here. Submitting a correction through GitHub
        publishes information according to that issue’s visibility; include only
        information you want to share publicly.
      </p>
      <h2>Agent Explainer</h2>
      <p>
        The linked lab stores theme and learning progress in your browser. Its
        scenarios are local simulations and do not call model APIs. Moving to a
        new domain does not transfer preferences stored for the previous domain.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
